<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="042" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-14 — adapt /bff-deploy for net10 + author the slot-swap runbook</title>
    <phase>P4 CI/CD + deploy plumbing</phase>
    <gate>041 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Writes .claude/skills/ (main-session-only) + the deploy runbook that governs the production cutover.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Skill + runbook authoring with exact az commands; well-specified by design §7.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Writes `.claude/skills/bff-deploy/**` — MAIN-SESSION-ONLY per root §3 sub-agent write boundary.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>041</deps>
    <tags>deployment, skill-directives, dotnet, migration</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Adapt the `/bff-deploy` skill so it no longer encodes the 8.0 runtime, and author a slot-swap cutover runbook with the EXACT `az` commands: create/refresh a staging slot, set `linuxFxVersion` to `DOTNETCORE|10.0` on the slot only (pipe form), deploy the net10 framework-dependent build, validate on the slot hostname, swap staging→production (atomic runtime+binary), and rollback-by-swap. Note the colon form `DOTNETCORE:10.0` for `az webapp create --runtime`/`list-runtimes`, the port-8080/no-hardcoded-ASPNETCORE_URLS rule, and that auto-swap is unsupported on Linux (manual/CLI/pipeline). This is a MAIN-SESSION-ONLY write task (`.claude/skills/`).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer + release engineer. Expert in Azure App Service staging slots, zero-downtime swaps, and Spaarke's /bff-deploy skill. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`.claude/skills/bff-deploy/**` no longer encodes 8.0; a runbook at `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/slot-swap-runbook.md` (and/or in the skill) gives the exact `az` command sequence for staging-slot deploy → validate → swap → rollback-by-swap, with the pipe/colon forms, port-8080, and Linux-no-auto-swap facts baked in.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec FR-14 + design §7. `/bff-deploy` currently encodes 8.0 assumptions. Design §7 gives the 6-step zero-downtime path + the hard facts (pipe vs colon; mismatch = 503; don't hardcode ASPNETCORE_URLS/UseUrls; don't pin RuntimeFrameworkVersion; auto-swap unsupported on Linux). The runbook is the operator's script for tasks 050/051/060/061. Writing `.claude/skills/` requires the main session (root §3).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">.claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/slot-swap-runbook.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="041" status="pending">IaC runtime strings updated (the runbook references DOTNETCORE|10.0).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">MAIN-SESSION-ONLY: edits `.claude/skills/bff-deploy/**` — a sub-agent CANNOT write there (root §3).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The runbook MUST include the exact `az` commands with the PIPE form (`DOTNETCORE|10.0`) for `linux-fx-version`/`config set` and the COLON form (`DOTNETCORE:10.0`) for `create`/`list-runtimes`; MUST document rollback = swap-back.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Deploy stays framework-dependent linux-x64 from `deploy/api-publish/`; MUST NOT hardcode `ASPNETCORE_URLS`/`UseUrls()` or pin `RuntimeFrameworkVersion`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Runtime + binary change atomically via the swap; the runbook must make this explicit.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Zero-downtime App Service slot-swap deploy for net10</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="slot-swap-sequence" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §7 — the 6-step zero-downtime path + hard facts.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-14 + design §7. Declare RIGOR: FULL. Confirm MAIN SESSION for the `.claude/skills/` write.</step>
    <step order="1">Update `/bff-deploy` SKILL.md: replace any 8.0 runtime assumption with net10; reference the runbook.</step>
    <step order="2">Author `notes/slot-swap-runbook.md`: the 6-step sequence with exact `az` commands (staging slot create/refresh; `az webapp config set --slot staging --linux-fx-version "DOTNETCORE|10.0"`; deploy; validate; swap; rollback-by-swap).</step>
    <step order="3">Bake in the hard facts: pipe vs colon; mismatch = 503; port 8080 / no hardcoded ASPNETCORE_URLS; no RuntimeFrameworkVersion pin; auto-swap unsupported on Linux (manual/CLI/pipeline).</step>
    <step order="4">Cross-check the runbook against `deploy-bff-api.yml` (task 040) so the pipeline + manual path agree.</step>
    <step order="5">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 042 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the current /bff-deploy skill encodes a deploy mechanism incompatible with the slot-swap path (e.g. deploys directly to production), STOP and surface per CLAUDE.md §6 — the cutover safety depends on the slot path; do not paper over an incompatible skill.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">n/a (docs/skill)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">.claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/slot-swap-runbook.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`/bff-deploy` no longer encodes the 8.0 runtime string.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The runbook contains the exact `az` command sequence with the pipe form for `linux-fx-version` and the colon form for `create`/`list-runtimes`, plus rollback-by-swap.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The runbook documents port-8080/no-hardcoded-ASPNETCORE_URLS, no-RuntimeFrameworkVersion-pin, and Linux-no-auto-swap.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: authored in the main session (not a sub-agent) — the `.claude/skills/` write succeeded.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-14. Main-session-only per root §3. The runbook is executed by the operator in tasks 050/051/060/061.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
